Syntax: pray 'expel' <target>

The Expel prayer safely removes embedded objects from a person's body using
divine intervention. Arrows, spear tips, and other foreign objects are
pushed out through the entry wound without causing the bleeding and tissue
damage that normally accompanies removal.

This prayer is invaluable for battlefield medicine. Manually removing
embedded objects typically causes severe bleeding and risks infection, but
expel extracts items cleanly through the power of faith. The object falls
to the ground once removed.

Important: Expel only removes the foreign object - it does not heal any
damage the item caused when it struck the victim. Wounds, broken bones,
and bleeding that existed before the prayer remain and require additional
healing. The prayer also does not sterilize the wound.

See Also: CLOT, STERILIZE, SALVE, KNIT BONE
